# 3. P0 FIX — SEPARATE PAPER AND LIVE EXECUTION

Currently, the engine incorrectly associates trade execution source with market-data source.

Remove this coupling completely.

A live Upstox market-data feed must not imply that a trade was actually executed on Upstox.

Implement independent execution pipelines.

Recommended architecture:

```text
CONFIRMED EMA SIGNAL
        |
        v
SIGNAL VALIDATION
        |
        v
EXECUTION COORDINATOR
        |
        +----------------------+
        |                      |
        v                      v
 PAPER PIPELINE          LIVE PIPELINE
        |                      |
        v                      v
PAPER ENABLED?           LIVE ENABLED?
        |                      |
        v                      v
SIMULATED ENTRY          SAFETY VALIDATION
        |                      |
        v                      v
PAPER POSITION           UPSTOX ORDER
        |                      |
        v                      v
PAPER SL/TP              BROKER RESPONSE
        |                      |
        v                      v
PAPER EXIT             FILL / REJECTION
        |                      |
        v                      v
PAPER P&L              LIVE POSITION IF FILLED
```

The two pipelines must never mutate each other's positions.

Refactor `processAutoPaperTrade()` into an execution coordinator with clearly separated operations.

Suggested responsibilities:

```typescript
processConfirmedSignal()

executePaperSignal()

attemptLiveSignal()

monitorPaperPositions()

monitorLivePositions()

requestPaperExit()

requestLiveExit()

reconcileLivePositions()
```

Do not merely rename the existing function.

Actually separate the underlying state, database records, execution dependencies, and broker interactions.

Preserve support for all four combinations:

| Paper | Live | Behavior |
|---|---|---|
| OFF | OFF | Signals only |
| ON | OFF | Paper execution only |
| OFF | ON | Live execution attempts only |
| ON | ON | Independent paper and live execution |

All four combinations must have automated tests.

